    "done_when": "Implement the lead's locked decision kernel-loop-representation = custom-derivative-rules on converged-forward-solve (2026-10-06): the Biot kernel point jet carries its own derivative rules, so autodiff no longer unrolls the differentiated harmonic recurrences, holding the 1e-13 identity against the base kernels. Measured cause (stop record docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-kernel-qualification.html#cfs-kernel-qualification-record): the traced topology read's expanded graph is about 1.5 million equations at 132, 300 and 550 cells alike, and value_gradient, the jax.jacfwd of the kernel point jet, contributes 99 percent of it; the read builds its Hessian in BiotMomentCoupling.evaluate (nova/equilibrium/topology.py, around line 2303) by jax.jacfwd of BiotMomentCoupling.value_gradient, which calls packed_analytic_moments (nova/biot/polygonanalytic.py:2363). Those nine rows already carry the flux and the field analytically (Psi, PsiR, PsiZ, Br, BrR, BrZ, Bz, BzR, BzZ), so the derivative of the flux rows with respect to the target point is already in the field rows; what autodiff unrolls is the derivative of the field rows. The existing custom_jvp pattern in nova/biot/greens.py (around line 184) is the house idiom. Done when: (1) the point jet that the read differentiates (value, gradient and Hessian of the booked-moment coupling at a target point, and the same for the filament source kind) is wrapped in a jax.custom_jvp whose tangent with respect to the target point is computed by closed-form or recurrence-form derivative rows of the field (the derivative of each harmonic recurrence written as its own recurrence, or the analytic second-derivative kernel where one exists in nova/biot), never by autodiff through the recurrences, with tangents with respect to the moments and source geometry either supplied the same way or shown to be linear and cheap; (2) identity: on 10,000 random target points spanning near-source and far-field distances for both source kinds, value, gradient and Hessian from the custom rule agree with the base-revision autodiff kernels to relative error at or below 1e-13 (print the maximum per component), the base kernels loaded through importlib from git show at the run's orientation_base_sha under a different module name, never copied into the tree; the third and fourth derivatives the read's curvature corrections take are checked the same way where the read takes them by autodiff; (3) negative control: the custom rule with one derivative recurrence truncated by one term fails the identity test, its maximum error printed; (4) compile: in fresh subprocesses with the persistent compilation cache disabled in the environment before jax is imported and the cache guard rows asserted as misses, the point jet's cold compile and the kernel-backed topology read at 132, 300 and 550 cells are compiled cold on the H200 with wall, unique and expanded equation counts, executable bytes and peak host RSS per rung, each row bounded at 900 s, in one job; (5) if the 550-cell read compiles cold at or below 60 s with an executable at or below 50 MB, a second job runs the 1074 and 2616 kernel-backed rows and the implicit kernel null tangent rows in tests/equilibrium/test_topology_read.py, and their strict expected-failure markers are removed only for rows that pass, each passing row asserting the 60 s and 50 MB bounds in its own body so a later slow compile fails rather than passes; if 550 exceeds the clause, no larger row runs and the evidence states the remaining dominating construct from the jaxpr; (6) the existing tests under tests/biot and tests/equilibrium/test_topology_read.py pass by delta against the base on compute (per-module fresh processes, junit per module, added failures zero or each added id named), and an evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-kernel-derivative-rules.html with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve carries one table of identity maxima, compile walls, equation counts, executable bytes and RSS per rung, job ids and gate commands, with reckon audit-doc at 0 errors. Figures, if any, go under docs/figures/kernel-derivative-rules, never under docs/figures/converged-forward-solve, which a peer node is rewriting. Gates run on the H200 through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path under the run directory named in the manifest) --wait -- (the targets of that step); any wait is declared with wait_probe sacct -n -X -P -j (job id) -o State and wait_terminal COMPLETED FAILED CANCELLED TIMEOUT OUT_OF_MEMORY NODE_FAIL, never exit:0; on a compute node uv is not invoked and the shared environment's interpreter runs directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run's worktree (orientation_worktree in the manifest); every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync; configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. No public signature in nova/biot or nova/equilibrium changes. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest before every job wait; the manifest's commits line lists every commit.",
